 you  hear about it after the fact when they  lose that they didn't have energy they  weren't ready to play typically it  happens to them on the road but earlier  this year they were flat in multiple of  their home games i think they figured  out their way past and they presumably  would be past it in the postseason  there's one team though that fascinates  me as a potential visitor to lambeau  field in january and that's the tampa  bay buccaneers remember all those years  where the buccaneers have never won a  game where the temperature at kickoff  was below 40 degrees well now they've  got tom brady the ultimate northeast  outdoor quarterback who has sworn off  ever living in the northeast again now  he's gotten a taste of tampa but if they  have to go to lambeau field  not that he can do all that much to  prepare his guys who may not be  accustomed to those conditions to deal  with it but he sets the shining example  for the rest of them and he's the last  guy on the roster who's going to be  deterred by the cold the wind the snow  the whatever they may encounter if they  have to play in green bay and they beat  the packers 38 to 10 in tampa  i mean who knows how it would play out  or anything mike but the one  you just said it you know i the one one  of the reasons why i did not include the  bucks  in what i was saying about the teams is  that okay look so they've been  practicing in the warm all year  look at all the guys on that team who  are used to playing in cold weather and  i'll take obviously tom brady  uh two of their receivers chris godwin  from penn state scotty miller from  bowling green i mean these are guys who  grew up  playing in cold weather it's not really  going to be  uh you know an earth shaker to them and  so i sort of look at this  and i say  i think tampa bay would be well suited  to go up there and play them you know  particularly  if they get on a little bit of a roll  and brady really gets great chemistry  with his receiving group  nine years ago the packers were 15-1  with the number one seed and the giants  went in in the divisional round and  stunned them so it's going to be an  interesting play-off field whoever the  number one seed is in the nfc that's it  for pft on yahoo sports we'll see you  next time  [Music]  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

